# 386MAX downgrade patch: sudleyplace source â†’ TASM 3.1 + TLINK build
#
# Applies to: https://github.com/sudleyplace/386MAX @ 1.15 (BOB 07 Apr 1997)
#             archived at devtools/386max.7z in this repo.
#
# What this patch does: applies the 12 sed rules from
# MAIN/build/scripts/xform.sed plus the P5 per-file surgeries from
# MAXBLD1.BAT, transforming MASM 5.10/6.0 idioms into forms TASM 3.1
# can parse. See todo/386max-build-downgrade.md for the full recipe
# and why each rule exists.
#
# What this patch does NOT do: the macro-scoped @@/@F/@B relabeling
# performed by xform.awk, or the bt-family symbol-size annotation
# performed by xform-bt.awk. Those transforms produce mechanical
# LBL_N label injections that would explode the diff to unreviewable
# size and are more reliably re-derived at build time. The MAXBLD1.BAT
# pipeline runs sed + xform-bt.awk + xform.awk together, so applying
# this patch alone WILL NOT produce assemblable output â€” it captures
# the human-readable source deltas for review, and the awk passes
# happen at build time.
#
# Directory layout expected: {KERNEL,INC}/ at patch root.
# KERNEL/ = original 386max-src/386MAX/ contents.
# INC/    = original 386max-src/INC/    contents.
#
# Files listed as removed (P5a, P5e) are deliberately skipped from the
# build entirely (QMAX_FLX.ASM has no `end` directive, QMAX_DIF.ASM has
# 100+ catstr/textmacro incompatibilities with TASM).
#
# Gate 1 status: 92/92 assemblies succeed, 386MAX.SYS produced at
# 235,224 bytes (102.60% of shipped Qualitas 229,268). Gate 2
# (load-verify under DEVICE=) pending â€” see roadmap doc.
#
# GPLv3, ours to redistribute alongside the built 386MAX.SYS.

